   "id": 632947,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"5\">\n  <li>The height, in meters, of a baseball being hit is modeled by the function <span data-math=\"h(x) = -2x^2+ 12x + 3\">h(x) = -2x^2+ 12x + 3</span> where <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> is the number of seconds since being hit.<br> <br> Approximately how many seconds pass before the baseball lands on the ground? Use graphing technology if needed.</li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [
